jobs.description:
As a Control Panel Builder, you will assemble and wire electrical control panels according to technical drawings and electrical schematics. You make sure that each panel is completed safely, accurately, and in line with the customer’s requirements.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Assembling control cabinets and operator panels;
- Mounting and wiring electrical components;
- Reading and working from electrical drawings and schematics;
- Checking and testing completed control panels;
- Occasionally supporting installation or service work at customer locations.

Most of your work will take place in the workshop, where you will work alongside a team of experienced technicians.

- Technical MBO diploma in Electrical Engineering or related field;
- Experience with control panel assembly is a plus;
- Ability to work from technical and electrical drawings;
- Detail-oriented and quality-focused mindset;
- Able to work independently and in a team;
- English communication skills required.

Are you technically minded and looking to work for a modern metal company with a great working atmosphere? Then this CNC Operator position could be the perfect job for you! What will you do?

What are you going to do?
Depending on your experience, you will work in one of several departments. Your tasks may include:

- Operating CNC turning or milling machines;
- Inspecting and measuring products;
- Reading technical drawings;
- Tack welding, finishing, or preparing products;
- Working with EDM (Electrical Discharge Machining).

You will be part of a close-knit team and responsible for maintaining product quality and ensuring a smooth production process. 

What do we offer?
- A gross monthly salary between €3,400 and €3,500 (excluding shift allowance);
- 25% shift allowance based on a full-time workweek of 38.75 hours;
- Excellent employment conditions and pension scheme under the Metalektro collective labour agreement;
- 27 vacation days and 13 additional leave (ADV) days;
- Travel allowance of €0.23 per kilometre;
- An informal and friendly working environment;
- Fun activities organised by the active staff association.

Where will you work?
You will join a modern metalworking company that manufactures high-quality components for the aerospace and energy industries. Together with approximately 140 colleagues, you will work with the latest technologies in an informal and supportive environment. You will have plenty of opportunities to develop yourself and become part of a close and committed team.

What do we ask?
- Experience in metalworking or engineering;
- CNC experience is an advantage;
- Ability to read technical drawings;
- Accuracy and a strong focus on quality;
- Able to work independently as well as in a team;
- You speak Dutch, German, or English.

You will work in a 3-shift rotation:

06:00 - 14:15

14:00 - 22:15

22:00 - 06:15

